A Python package whose implementation is a Rust extension (PyO3, built by maturin).

## Layout

- `crates/core/` - pure-Rust logic, no Python dependency; unit tests beside the code
- `crates/py/` - thin PyO3 bindings, compiled to `{{ package_name }}._core`
- `src/{{ package_name }}/` - the Python package: re-exports, `_core.pyi` stubs, `py.typed`
- `tests/` - pytest suite that exercises the built extension
- `docs/` - MkDocs site; the API page is generated from the built extension, so Python docstrings are the `///` comments on each `#[pyfunction]`

## Commands

Use `just` (bare `just` lists the recipes), `uv run` and `cargo`; never `pip`,
`maturin develop` or a bare `python`.

- `just check` - format check, clippy + ruff, ty, Rust and Python tests. **Work is not done until this passes.**
- `just test-rust name_filter` / `just test-py -k name` - run one side while iterating
- `uv add <pkg>` / `cargo add -p {{ project_name }}-core <crate>` - change dependencies; run `just deny` after Rust changes

## Verification

- Logic changes need a Rust test in `crates/core`; anything visible from Python
  also needs a pytest test. Tests must fail before the change and pass after.
- Hooks format every edit and run `just check` when you finish.
- Clippy runs with `pedantic` and `-D warnings`, ruff with every rule. Do not
  add `#[allow(...)]`, `# noqa` or `# type: ignore` to get green; configure
  the rule in `Cargo.toml` / `pyproject.toml` with a reason.
- Prefer the language servers (rust-analyzer, ty) over text search for navigation.

## Gotchas

- `uv run` rebuilds the extension when Rust sources change (`cache-keys` in
  `pyproject.toml`), so Python tests always see current Rust code. A new
  non-`.rs` build input must be added to `cache-keys`.
- A function exposed to Python changes in three places: `crates/py/src/lib.rs`,
  the type stub `src/{{ package_name }}/_core.pyi`, and the re-export in `__init__.py`.
- The version lives only in `[workspace.package]` in the root `Cargo.toml`.
- `crates/py` has no Rust tests by design (a test binary would need libpython).
- `.cargo/config.toml` points PyO3 at `.venv/bin/python`, so cargo commands
  need `just setup` first.
